https://prominent.itch.io/crocotile3d
Simple tool that lets you make 3d scenes and models in a 2d tile style, reminiscent of games like Mario 64 or Quake
Pros:
Helps you easily make a very specific style of graphics 
Has a lot of polished modern graphics capabilities like lighting and reflections
Cons:
Very limited beyond it’s very niche style

https://lexaloffle.itch.io/pico-8
Immersive “fantasy console” that lets you fully create and run games in engine using lua
Pros:
Extremely unique stylized feeling
Restrictions for simplicity can drive creativity
Community minded system of “carts” to allow you to easily share games, pushes people to make small simple projects rather than large over the top games
Entirely contained game development tools in IDE
Cons:
Restrictions can limit your capability

https://microstudio.itch.io/microstudio
Well rounded game engine with contained tools for programming, asset development, and testing, reminiscent of a more complex scratch
Pros:
Easy to learn
2d and 3d
Has everything you need in theory
Cons:
Doesn’t really do anything something like Unity couldn’t do better, just less complex





https://baj.itch.io/drafft
Visual programming style game planner that helps you track dialogue, storylines, as well as keep all your files organized and track your progress with the project
Pros:
Intuitive programming inspired flow chart
Can do a lot for just one tool
Collaborative work implemented
Cons:
Seemingly no support for Github

https://johanpeitz.itch.io/picocad
Tool built with Pico-8 that lets you make 3d models in a very similar, stylized, restricted fashion as Pico-8
Pros:
Limitations can drive creativity
Very stylized workspace
Cons:
Limitations

https://unity.com/
Extremely popular game engine with very wide variety, very popular with indie games
Pros:
Well made engine that lets you focus on the game itself
Very well supported and documented


Cons:
Struggles with very high end games


https://www.unrealengine.com/
Very powerful game engine used in some of the largest games as of late
Pros:
Very good with graphics
Let’s you make very complex games
Widely accepted industry standard
Cons:
IDE itself doesn’t perform well on lower end machines
Much more complex
Graphics can tend to all look the same across games

https://www.blender.org/
By far the most widely used 3d modeling software for creative projects
Pros:
Very powerful in capability
Open-source
Cons:
Steep learning curve
Low performance in very complex environments

https://godotengine.org/
Open source game engine for 2d and 3d that let’s you do a lot
Pros:
Open source license for publishing
Lightweight
Customizable
Cons:
Can struggle with complex projects

https://www.jetbrains.com/clion
C/C++ IDE developed by Jetbrains that is primarily used for Java and Javascript but has a version for C
Pros:
Nice tools
Clean design
Easy plugins and compatibility
Cons:
Doesn’t always perform well
Limited features without subscription or student license



